.mcp.json
.playwright-mcp/

# Android shell (feat/android-shell) - www/ is generated by scripts/build-www.js
# from the canonical web source; node_modules is npm-managed tooling. Neither
# is a second copy of the app and neither should be committed.
node_modules/
www/

# Generated visual test captures and exploratory RT7 branding previews.
# Keep established branding source assets trackable.
artifacts/
branding/resin-tools/rt7-*

# Theme Lab (developer-only tool) writes timestamped theme.css backups here.
tools/theme-lab/backups/

# Subagent project memory (.claude/agents/*.md declare `memory: project`).
# Useful locally, but it is derived notes an agent writes about its own
# findings - it grows unprompted and nothing reviews it the way code gets
# reviewed. One entry here had already recorded a passing test as "flaky"
# when it was simply reading node_modules from a worktree that had none.
# Keep it out of history so a bad note stays a local annoyance; the agent
# definitions themselves are tracked, in .claude/agents/.
.claude/agent-memory/
